      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T18:46:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both ZLP `DFU_DOWNLOAD` failure (`ret \u003c 0`, lines 428–433) and manifestation poll failure (`!dfu_poll_idle()`, lines 443–447) must fail the download rather than printing a warning and returning success:\n- RTS5817 performs partition-length validation (e.g., rejecting an unpadded binary whose size does not match `dwTotalFWLen`) and whole-image SHA-256 verification inside the final zero-length `DFU_DNLOAD(wLength \u003d 0)` handler. When verification fails, the device `STALL`s the ZLP (`LIBUSB_ERROR_PIPE`), transitions to `bStatus \u003d errNOTDONE (9)` / `bState \u003d dfuERROR (10)`, and omits writing the firmware-valid flag — leaving the SPI flash partition unbootable.\n- Because RTS5817 sets `bitManifestationTolerant \u003d 1` (`bmAttributes \u003d 0x0F`), a valid flash on RTS5817 always ACKs the ZLP and reaches `bState \u003d dfuIDLE (2)` on `DFU_GETSTATUS` without disconnecting mid-manifestation.\n\nSwallowing these errors causes `rts5817_flash` to print `\"Flash completed successfully.\"` and exit `0` even when flash verification failed and the device cannot boot. Please return an error on both paths (releasing `dfu_interface_`, and if the ZLP `STALL`s, optionally querying `DFU_GETSTATUS` / `DFU_CLRSTATUS` first so the device\u0027s `bStatus` code is surfaced in the error). Also verify that post-ZLP polling specifically reaches `dfuIDLE (2)` rather than `dfuDNLOAD-IDLE (5)`.",
