      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T19:06:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After manifestation reaches `dfuIDLE (2)`, the host still needs to send `DFU_DETACH` (`bmRequestType \u003d 0x21`, `bRequest \u003d 0x00`, `wIndex \u003d dfu_interface_`) so the RTS5817 exits DFU mode and boots the newly flashed image:\n- Because RTS5817 sets `bitManifestationTolerant \u003d 1` and `bitWillDetach \u003d 1` (`bmAttributes \u003d 0x0F`), `DFU_GETSTATUS` transitions `dfuMANIFEST-SYNC (6) -\u003e dfuIDLE (2)` and never enters `dfuMANIFEST-WAIT-RESET (8)` (so `backend_-\u003ereset_device()` in `dfu_poll_idle()` is never reached).\n- RTS5817 persists its DFU state across warm resets in an always-on register (`R_AL_DUMMY0`); only receiving `DFU_DETACH` while in DFU mode clears that state back to `appIDLE`, resets `R_INITVTOR`, and triggers a chip reset into the new firmware (`0BDA:5817`).\n\nPlease either send this post-manifest `DFU_DETACH` here before releasing `dfu_interface_` (with unit test coverage), or document clearly that callers must invoke `dfu_detach()` after `dfu_download()` succeeds.",
